/-!
# Uniform asymptotics of scaled exponential partial sums

For integer order `n` and real argument `x ≤ 1 - δ` (`δ > 0`), the partial sums
`e_n(n x) = ∑_{k ≤ n} (n x)^k / k!` of the exponential series satisfy Buckholtz's uniform
asymptotic expansion (DLMF 8.11.18–8.11.19)
`∑_{k ≤ n} (n x)^k / k! = e^{n x} - ((n x)^n / n!) (∑_{k < m} d_k(x) / n^k + O(n^{-m}))`
uniformly for `x ∈ (-∞, 1 - δ]`, where the rational coefficient functions `d_k` are generated by
`d_0(x) = x / (1 - x)` and `d_{k+1}(x) = -(x / (1 - x)) d_k'(x)`.

Through the Erlang identity `1 - P(n + 1, z) = e^{-z} ∑_{k ≤ n} z^k / k!`
(`TauCeti.regularizedGamma_natCast`), this gives the uniform large-parameter expansion of
`TauCeti.regularizedGamma (n + 1) (n * x)` on `[0, 1 - δ]`, complementing the central diagonal
expansions at `x = 1` (DLMF 8.11.12–8.11.17). Writing
`d_k(z) = (-1)^k z p_k(z) / (1 - z)^{2k + 1}` exhibits integer numerator polynomials
`p_k ∈ ℤ[X]` (`TauCeti.expPartialSumPoly`) with nonnegative coefficients satisfying `p_0 = 1` and
`p_{k+1}(X) = (1 + 2k X) p_k(X) + X (1 - X) p_k'(X)`, whose reflection `p_k(-X)` is the polynomial
sequence `A_k` governing the large-order uniform expansion of the generalized exponential integral
`E_p(λ p)` (DLMF 8.20.4–8.20.6).

The expansion is proved without splitting across the Szegő curve `|x e^{1 - x}| = 1`: starting
from the exact Taylor integral remainder
`e^z - ∑_{k ≤ n} z^k / k! = z^{n + 1} / n! * ∫₀¹ (1 - s)^n e^{z s} ds`, setting `z = n w`
(`Re w < 1`) expresses the normalized remainder after `m` integrations by parts against
`-∂_s ((1 - s)^n e^{n w s}) = n (1 - w (1 - s)) (1 - s)^{n - 1} e^{n w s}` as an integral of
`d_m(w (1 - s))` against a kernel of unit integral. For real `x < 1` this kernel is a probability
density on `[0, 1]`, yielding both an explicit uniform remainder bound on `(-∞, 1 - δ]` (and on
complex wedges `{w : ℂ | Re w ≤ 1 - δ ∧ |Im w| ≤ M * (1 - Re w)}`) and strict enveloping bounds by
the first neglected term on `[0, 1)`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.expPartialSumPoly`: the numerator polynomial sequence `p_k ∈ ℤ[X]` satisfying
  `p_0 = 1` and `p_{k+1}(X) = (1 + 2k X) p_k(X) + X (1 - X) p_k'(X)`.
* `TauCeti.expPartialSumCoeff`: the rational coefficient sequence
  `d_k(z) = (-1)^k z p_k(z) / (1 - z)^{2k + 1}` of DLMF 8.11.18–8.11.19 over any field.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.eval_one_expPartialSumPoly`, `TauCeti.natDegree_expPartialSumPoly`,
  `TauCeti.leadingCoeff_expPartialSumPoly`, `TauCeti.one_le_aeval_expPartialSumPoly`,
  `TauCeti.comp_neg_X_expPartialSumPoly_succ`: degree `k - 1`, leading coefficient `k!`, value
  `(2k - 1)‼` at `1`, positivity on `[0, ∞)`, and the DLMF 8.20.4 recurrence for `p_k(-X)`.
* `TauCeti.hasDerivAt_expPartialSumCoeff`, `TauCeti.expPartialSumCoeff_succ_eq_neg_div_mul_deriv`,
  `TauCeti.eq_expPartialSumCoeff_of_recurrence`: the differential recurrence
  `d_{k+1}(z) = -(z / (1 - z)) d_k'(z)` of DLMF 8.11.19 and its uniqueness off `z = 1`.
* `Complex.exp_sub_sum_range_succ_eq_integral`, `Real.exp_sub_sum_range_succ_eq_integral`,
  `Complex.exp_mul_sub_sum_range_succ_eq_sum_add_integral`,
  `TauCeti.exp_mul_sub_sum_range_succ_eq_sum_add_integral`: exact Taylor and `m`-fold
  integration-by-parts remainder identities on `Re w < 1` and `x < 1`.
* `TauCeti.abs_sum_range_succ_div_factorial_sub_le`,
  `TauCeti.isBigO_sum_range_succ_div_factorial_sub`,
  `TauCeti.isBigO_div_exp_sub_sum_range_succ_sub`,
  `TauCeti.isBigO_sum_range_succ_div_factorial_sub_of_recurrence`: explicit uniform remainder bound
  and DLMF 8.11.18 uniformly on `(-∞, 1 - δ]` (`atTop ×ˢ 𝓟 (Iic (1 - δ))`), together with
  `Complex.isBigO_sum_range_succ_div_factorial_sub` on complex wedges.
* `TauCeti.neg_one_pow_mul_integral_sub_sum_nonneg`, `TauCeti.neg_one_pow_mul_integral_sub_sum_le`,
  `TauCeti.isBigO_regularizedGamma_natCast_add_one_mul_sub`,
  `TauCeti.regularizedGamma_natCast_add_one_mul_isEquivalent`: strict enveloping bounds on `[0, 1)`
  and uniform asymptotic expansions of `TauCeti.regularizedGamma (n + 1) (n * x)` on `[0, 1 - δ]`.

## References

* *NIST Digital Library of Mathematical Functions*, [§8.11(v)](https://dlmf.nist.gov/8.11#v),
  Eqs. 8.11.18 and 8.11.19, and [§8.20(ii)](https://dlmf.nist.gov/8.20#ii), Eqs. 8.20.4–8.20.5.
* J. D. Buckholtz, *Concerning an approximation of Copson*, Proc. Amer. Math. Soc. **14** (1963),
  564–568.
* F. G. Tricomi, *Asymptotische Eigenschaften der unvollständigen Gammafunktion*, Math. Z. **53**
  (1950), 136–148.
* N. M. Temme, *Special Functions: An Introduction to the Classical Functions of Mathematical
  Physics*, Wiley, 1996, §11.2.
-/

